    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>Build the main simple version of a frontend layout for RoomRadar QC, including a navigation bar that allows users to move between the main page.</p>

<p>The navigation bar should include links to:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Home</li>
	<li>Find Rooms</li>
	<li>Login</li>
	<li>Admin Upload</li>
</ul>


<p>Done when:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Navbar component is created</li>
	<li>Navbar is visible on all pages</li>
	<li>Navigation links work correctly</li>
	<li>RoomRadar QC branding/title is shown</li>
	<li>Layout looks clean and consistent</li>
</ul>

            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <br/>

    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
            &nbsp;<font color="#ffffff"><b>Comments</b></font>&nbsp;
        </td>
        <td>&nbsp;</td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="grid" style="margin: 0;">
                <tr id="comment-header-10069"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:10757065-3ef5-4327-949d-84ace9a6dc0e"
                id="word_commented_712020:10757065-3ef5-4327-949d-84ace9a6dc0e"
                href="https://kyrilousnasr.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A10757065-3ef5-4327-949d-84ace9a6dc0e">
                    Joseph Uwagba
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">03/May/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-10069"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>This is a solid start for the frontend layout. The navbar clearly includes all the required links (Home, Find Rooms, Login, Admin Upload), which makes navigation straightforward for users. The RoomRadar QC branding is also visible, which helps with identity and consistency across pages.</p>

<p>Make sure the navbar is properly reused across all pages (not duplicated manually) so updates are easier later. Also confirm that each link routes correctly ( <tt>/</tt>, <tt>/find-rooms</tt>, <tt>/login</tt>, <tt>/admin-upload</tt>) and doesn’t cause full page reloads if using React Router.</p>

<p>From a design perspective, the layout looks clean, but consider adding a hover effect or active state on the navbar links so users know which page they’re on. Also, I will test responsiveness to ensure the navbar works well on smaller screens.</p>
        </td></tr>
            </table>
<hr class='fullcontent'><br /><br style='page-break-before:always;'/><br />
