    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>RoomDetails page is mostly implemented. It is reachable at <tt>/rooms/:id</tt>, shows room name/building, displays schedule info, has a back button, and matches the app style. However, it still uses mock data and has some text encoding issues.</p>

<p><b>Issues:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Uses hardcoded room/schedule data instead of backend data.</li>
	<li>Unknown room IDs show the first room instead of an error.</li>
	<li>Text has broken characters like <tt>â€¢</tt>, <tt>â€”</tt>, and <tt>Todayâ€™s</tt>.</li>
	<li>Does not show availability details from the selected room yet.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Suggested Fixes:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Connect RoomDetails to backend data.</li>
	<li>Add not-found/error state.</li>
	<li>Fix broken text characters.</li>
	<li>Show availability details from search results.</li>
</ul>

            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

